@codelaw/rules-security-ts

Every rule in this pack is written for codelaw, in its own words, from the documentation of the
frameworks it covers (Angular, NestJS, Next.js, tRPC, Prisma, TypeORM, Drizzle, Kysely, MikroORM)
and the OWASP cheat sheets. No rule is ported from another tool and no source code, pattern or
documentation text is copied.

Rule sets under a copyleft or source-available licence — eslint-plugin-no-unsanitized
(MPL-2.0), njsscan (LGPL-3.0), Semgrep's rules (the Semgrep Rules License) — are
read for ideas only; no text, pattern or code is taken from them (L2). CodeQL's JavaScript queries
(MIT) were read for ideas; nothing is copied.
